1. Causal-Forcing
   https://github.com/thu-ml/Causal-Forcing
   Apache License, Version 2.0. Copyright the Causal-Forcing authors.

   third_party/causal_forcing_overlay/ holds modified versions of files of Causal-Forcing at commit
   3e7cc998e745afd439d5b691e30b8a4a5d48ce38 and two added files. scripts/setup/setup_causal_forcing.sh copies them
   over a checkout of that commit; Causal-Forcing itself is not redistributed in this repository. All files in
   third_party/causal_forcing_overlay/ are licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (full text in
   third_party/LICENSE-Apache-2.0.txt), not under the S-Lab License. Every modified file carries a notice. The
   changes are:
     model/base.py                        build the text encoder and VAE of the configured model (Wan2.2-TI2V-5B)
     model/diffusion.py                   teacher-forcing loss on variable-length videos with validity masks,
                                          per-sample seeded training noise, Wan2.2 loss weighting
     pipeline/causal_diffusion_inference.py  Wan2.2-TI2V-5B dimensions, KV caches sized to the video,
                                          segment-wise sampling helpers used by the rollout engine
     trainer/__init__.py                  export the diffusion trainer only
     trainer/diffusion.py                 warmup with cosine / constant schedules and resets on resume, exact
                                          full-state resume, variable-length bucketed data, paired training noise,
                                          FSDP2 options
     utils/dataset.py                     variable-length latent LMDB datasets with metadata, length-bucketed samplers
     utils/distributed.py                 FSDP2, tensor- and sequence-parallel helpers
     utils/wan_wrapper.py                 Wan2.2-TI2V-5B support (48-channel Wan2.2 VAE through diffusers, model
                                          folders) and KV-cache arguments for segment-wise generation
     wan/modules/attention.py             PyTorch scaled-dot-product fallback when FlashAttention is missing
     wan/modules/causal_model.py          teacher-forcing attention masks for K-frame segments on a clean history
                                          (FlexAttention), variable-length buckets, KV-cache inference
     wan/modules/model.py                 Wan2.2 "ti2v" model type, head counts of sharded projections
     utils/sequence_parallel.py (added)   Ulysses sequence parallelism
     utils/tp_parallel.py (added)         tensor parallelism

   Causal-Forcing builds on Self-Forcing and on Wan. The files under wan/ keep the notice
   "Copyright 2024-2025 The Alibaba Wan Team Authors. All rights reserved." and the Apache License, Version 2.0.

